🛡️ Wazuh Active Response – SSH Brute Force Detection Lab
📌 Project Overview

This lab demonstrates detection and automatic mitigation of SSH brute-force attacks using Wazuh Active Response.

An attacker machine (Kali Linux) attempted multiple failed SSH logins against an Ubuntu server monitored by a Wazuh agent. After 5 failed attempts, Wazuh triggered an Active Response to automatically block the attacker’s IP.

🧰 Lab Environment

Wazuh Server

Ubuntu Server (Wazuh Agent installed)

Kali Linux (Attacker machine)

🔍 Attack Simulation

SSH brute-force attempt using incorrect credentials

Log generated in /var/log/auth.log

Wazuh rule triggered (SSH failed login rule)

Active Response executed

Attacker IP blocked automatically


🧠 Skills Demonstrated

SIEM configuration (Wazuh)

Log analysis

SSH attack detection

Active Response configuration

Firewall automation

Incident response validation

🚀 Outcome

After 5 failed login attempts, the attacking IP was automatically blocked and could no longer access the target server.

